  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>K</mi></mfenced></math> of an object is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>K</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Following equation (1), for the two given bodies, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
